// spec: a function defined twice is an error at the second definition, as in C++ ([basic.def.odr]), also when the two spell one parameter type two ways that Kpp makes one (`long` is `int`, `signed char` is `char`: design.md, "Types"), never two bodies the code generator emits
// factorio: found by the templates thread comparing overload choices against clang: `int f(int)` beside `int f(long)` reached clang as two definitions of `f(int32)` ("clang rejected module"), and two definitions of one signature likewise
// error: function_defined_twice_is_error.kpp:7: error: the function twice is defined twice (first at line 6)
// error: function_defined_twice_is_error.kpp:9: error: the function wide is defined twice (first at line 8)
// error: function_defined_twice_is_error.kpp:11: error: the function narrow is defined twice (first at line 10)
int twice(int v) { return v; }
int twice(int v) { return v + 1; }
int wide(int v) { return 1; }
int wide(long v) { return 2; }
int narrow(char v) { return 1; }
int narrow(signed char v) { return 2; }
int declaredThenDefined(int v);
int declaredThenDefined(int v) { return v; }
int main()
{
  return twice(1) + wide(1) + narrow('a') + declaredThenDefined(1);
}
